' ============================================================================
' 36 One join and one projection: the matrix product of two small tensors.
'
' Source of Figure TL2 in ../tensor-logic/concepts.md (section 3). The figure
' restates the join and the projection of the paper (Domingos 2025, p. 5)
' on the numbers U = [[1, 2], [3, 4]] and V = [[5, 6], [7, 8]]. It adds no
' new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. U has the indices a and b, and V has the indices b and c.
'   2. The join multiplies U and V where the shared index b agrees, and it
'      keeps every index: a tensor with the indices a, b and c.
'   3. The projection onto a and c sums over b. The result is U V.
'   4. The equation W[a, c] = U[a, b] V[b, c] writes both steps. For two
'      Boolean relations, the step function after the sum gives their
'      composition.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 36-tl-join-projection.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 36-tl-join-projection
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam RectangleBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam nodesep 50
skinparam ranksep 45
title One join and one projection: W[a, c] = U[a, b] V[b, c]

rectangle U $rrs_storage [
**U[a, b]**
|= |= b = 0 |= b = 1 |
|= a = 0 | 1 | 2 |
|= a = 1 | 3 | 4 |
]

rectangle V $rrs_storage [
**V[b, c]**
|= |= c = 0 |= c = 1 |
|= b = 0 | 5 | 6 |
|= b = 1 | 7 | 8 |
]

rectangle JOIN $rrs_tl_engine [
**Join** <latex>(U \bowtie V)_{abc} = U_{ab} \, V_{bc}</latex>
|= a |= b |= c |= value |
| 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 · 5 = 5 |
| 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 · 6 = 6 |
| 0 | 1 | 0 | 2 · 7 = 14 |
| 0 | 1 | 1 | 2 · 8 = 16 |
| 1 | 0 | 0 | 3 · 5 = 15 |
| 1 | 0 | 1 | 3 · 6 = 18 |
| 1 | 1 | 0 | 4 · 7 = 28 |
| 1 | 1 | 1 | 4 · 8 = 32 |
]

rectangle PROJ $rrs_tl_engine [
**Projection onto a and c** <latex>\pi^{+}_{ac}(T)(a, c) = \sum_{b} T(a, b, c)</latex>
|= |= c = 0 |= c = 1 |
|= a = 0 | 5 + 14 = 19 | 6 + 16 = 22 |
|= a = 1 | 15 + 28 = 43 | 18 + 32 = 50 |
]

U -[$rrs_flow]-> JOIN : the factor U
V -[$rrs_flow]-> JOIN : the factor V
JOIN -[$rrs_effect]-> PROJ : sum over b, the index\nthat the left side does not name

note right of PROJ
  The result is the matrix product U V.
  For Boolean relations, the step function H
  after the sum gives their composition:
  Grandparent(x, z) <- Parent(x, y), Parent(y, z)
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_storage>   | input tensors |
|<$rrs_tl_engine> | the steps of the TL engine |
endlegend
@enduml
